<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n73380" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὅμᾰδ-ος</span></b> , ὁ, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>noise, din,</i> esp. of the
			confused voices of a number of men (coupled with <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δοῦπος,</span> the tramp of men), <i><span class="en">
				Il.
				9.573
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				23.234
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Od.
				10.556
			</span></i> (nowh. else in <i><span class="en">
				Od.
			</span></i>) ; also opp. the sound of flutes and pipes, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">συρίγγων τ᾽ ἐνοπὴν ὅμαδόν τ᾽
					ἀνθρώπων</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					10.13
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Pi.
				<u>N.</u>
				6.38
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Philyll.
				5
			</span></i> (lyr.) ; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὅ. ἄλυρον ἔλεγον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>Hel.</u>
					185
				</span></i>
			 (lyr.) ; rarely of a tempest, <i><span class="en">
				Il.
				13.797
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>noisy throng</i> or <i>mob of warriors,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				7.307
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				15.689
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				17.380
			</span></i>: metaph., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">βίβλων ὅ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pl.
					<u>R.</u>
					364e
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>III.</b>
			<i>din of battle,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Hes.
				<u>Sc.</u>
				155
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				257
			</span></i> ; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χάλκεον στονόεντ᾽ . . ὅμαδον</span>
			<i>the din</i> of brazen war, <i><span class="en">
				Pi.
				<u>I.</u>
				8(7).27
			</span></i>.—
				Ep.
			 and Lyr., never in Trag., exc. in <i><span class="en">
				E.
			</span></i> l. c. (lyr.), once in Pl.l.c.</div>
